# Aethora lore lock

The curated lore in `docs/terminology.md` and `docs/lore/` is the leading truth for **Brightcall**.

## Before any lore or GDD change

1. If the user says something that **conflicts** with locked Aethora lore, **stop and check** with them before editing. Do not silently overwrite the lock.
2. Write **English only** in all docs, even if the user prompt is in another language.
3. **Overwrite** outdated paragraphs. Do not annotate corrections. Do not keep “formerly called X” or “do not call it Y” in narrative.
4. Affirmative prose only: state what the world **is**.
5. Forget retired names in story text. Legacy words live only in terminology’s retired list.

## Locked pillars (summary)

- Game: **Brightcall** (one word)
- World: **Aethora** · Anomaly: **The Bright** (vast **cube** of light; interior monolithic maze; brighter = stronger Bright energy toward Core)
- **Eclipse:** the six faces — outside bright/see-in; inside dark smoky barrier
- **Umbra:** darkest weak spot on a face = dark doorway **entry only** (also mid-match Stitching return)
- Exit: none while Bright stands — only **Null-Flint harvest** (extract Core into containment) or **Null-Flint destroy** (shatter Core into Splinters) → implosion → Stitching to Eclipse crossing
- Monoliths/gates/walls: Bright’s defense — protect Core and trap the called
- Two energies: **Chroma** / Tears (Seam edges only; Magenta/Cyan/Searing Gold) · **Bright energy** (Core emission; causes Seams)
- The Bright feeds on Chroma; it does **not** eject Chroma; hungers for living matter; **quiets on organic material**; **violent while consuming Harvesters** (takes time; energy spent erupts as Seams that wrap prey)
- **Seams:** razor-thin satin / fractured-glass; **Chroma burst at eruption** + **continuous weep**; terrain/objects restore when curtain ends; Harvester or weapon wrap = **Enhancement**; **Bloom** only if Chroma enters body internally; external Chroma = damage only
- **Splinters:** Bright-powered Null-Flint formed when Null-Flint violently meets a Core (smash-harvest or shatter); crush/destroy → **synthetic Seam**; **Splinter-Crush** chambers (Refract pioneered) wrap weapons as Enhancements; table path = **Splintered** deck
- Perspectives: Kho'Lan = living predator / stomach / digestive Seams; Lumari = divine will; Kardia/Aureate/Refract = industrial reality-disruption science (quantum model still open — do not lock yet); Refract = Bright as volatile resource to exploit / study / weaponize
- Industrial trio: Kardia = Bright cells (stable power); Aureate = raw Chroma-fuel (brute force); Refract = synthetic Seam weaponry
- **Core:** reverse black hole of light; Seams crowd it; interior unknown; **Harvest** = take the Core (faction motives differ)
- **Call of the Bright** / **the calling:** pull toward Core; manifestation unknown (none heard and lived)
- **Brilliance:** pearl white, faintly radiant (Kardia); metal allows safe Chroma handling; **Bright cells** hold bright-white Bright energy; **Zenith Relays** are civic energy substations
- **Kardia do not deal in Tears/Chroma** as a resource; Vesper scratches that weep Tears are frowned upon
- **Oru:** very large; black stone-glimmer skin; hero-harvester plate is leading
- **Scratch:** Seam almost opening
- Factions: Kho'Lan, Lumari, Kardia, Refract Labs, the Aureate, Adumbra (Aureate: controlled Bloom infantry; barons rarely enter The Bright; Lumari: excess Bloom)
- Aesthetic: Bright-punk Fantasy genre label — civic-modern magitech + anomaly physics; Bone/Ash/Greige, Bruised Darkness, toxic neon Chroma; Bright energy reads bright white
- Refract: Splinter-Crush + Chroma research; no Core containment / Brilliance / Zenith Relays
- Eras: First Light → Traveling Light → Resting Light
- Match mutation: Splintered · No Weld
- Retired: Brightforged; Vertex Labs / Axiom Labs (use Refract Labs); intermittent bright-face walk-out exit

